  "findings": [
    "With identical CE batches, adding the candidate preference loss improves fixed-test top-1 by 9 and independent top-1 by 6 versus CE-only continuation. This is a modest gain, not a consistent win over deployment.",
    "Of the original 160 regressions, CE-only restores 45 and ranking restores 49. Across the full fixed set, ranking fixes 96 but creates 80 regressions.",
    "Independent entity examples: baseline 255/384, CE-only 255/384, ranking 249/384. Idioms: 363, 363, 367. Candidate ranking gains do not preserve all entity-name decisions.",
    "Independent whole compositions remain 394/640 versus baseline 402; ranking singles improve to 575/640 versus 573 and suffixes to 477/640 versus 476."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Phrase coverage counts are before augmentation and sampling; actual unique sampled rows are reported separately. Coverage does not establish the cause of an individual recovery.",
    "Ranking augmentation preserves source-row endpoints, but original source windows may already truncate a phrase. Automatic pronunciations and observed-text labels can still be ambiguous.",
    "Frozen labels were not edited. Held-out documents, normalized context/answer pairs and long overlaps were excluded from training. CE test ablation was post-hoc and did not revise checkpoint selection.",
    "Evaluation suites ran concurrently; their timings are not a deployment latency benchmark."
  ],
